---
import PolicyPageLayout from '../components/PolicyPageLayout.astro';
import { legalConfig } from '../data/legal';

const toc = [
  { id: 'responsible', label: 'Who is responsible for your personal data?' },
  { id: 'data-collected', label: 'What personal data we collect' },
  { id: 'calculator-data', label: 'Calculator data' },
  { id: 'uses', label: 'How we use personal data' },
  { id: 'legal-bases', label: 'Legal bases' },
  { id: 'required-information', label: 'Required and optional information' },
  { id: 'attachments', label: 'Attachments' },
  { id: 'recipients', label: 'Service providers and recipients' },
  { id: 'turnstile', label: 'Cloudflare Turnstile' },
  { id: 'google-workspace', label: 'Google Workspace' },
  { id: 'international-transfers', label: 'International data transfers' },
  { id: 'retention', label: 'Data retention' },
  { id: 'security', label: 'Security' },
  { id: 'rights', label: 'Your rights' },
  { id: 'automated-decisions', label: 'Automated decision-making' },
  { id: 'third-party-links', label: 'Third-party links' },
  { id: 'changes', label: 'Changes to this policy' },
] as const;
---

<PolicyPageLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | All Yacht Service"
  description="Learn how All Yacht Service handles personal data submitted through enquiries, attachments, calculators and website security services."
  heading="Privacy Policy"
  intro="This notice explains how personal data is handled when you contact All Yacht Service, use a calculator, submit files or interact with website security services."
  pathname="/privacy-policy"
  routeId="privacyPolicy"
  toc={toc}
>
  <section id="responsible" aria-labelledby="responsible-heading">
    <h2 id="responsible-heading">
      1. Who Is Responsible for Your Personal Data?
    </h2>
    {
      legalConfig.legalOperatorName ? (
        <p>
          The legal operator named below is responsible for the personal data
          described in this notice.
        </p>
      ) : (
        <p>
          The final legal identity of the website operator is being confirmed
          and will be added before this website is made indexable. The following
          public contact details are verified:
        </p>
      )
    }
    <dl class="policy-facts">
      {
        legalConfig.legalOperatorName && (
          <div>
            <dt>Legal operator</dt>
            <dd>{legalConfig.legalOperatorName}</dd>
          </div>
        )
      }
      {
        legalConfig.operatorType === 'natural-person' && (
          <div>
            <dt>Operator status</dt>
            <dd>Natural person</dd>
          </div>
        )
      }
      {
        legalConfig.legalForm && (
          <div>
            <dt>Legal form</dt>
            <dd>{legalConfig.legalForm}</dd>
          </div>
        )
      }
      <div><dt>Trading name</dt><dd>{legalConfig.tradingName}</dd></div>
      <div>
        <dt>Contact address</dt><dd>{legalConfig.publicOfficeAddress}</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Email</dt><dd>
          <a href={`mailto:${legalConfig.email}`}>{legalConfig.email}</a>
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Phone</dt><dd>
          <a href="tel:+34695718540">{legalConfig.phone}</a>
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Website</dt><dd>
          <a href={legalConfig.websiteUrl}>{legalConfig.websiteUrl}</a>
        </dd>
      </div>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <section id="data-collected" aria-labelledby="data-collected-heading">
    <h2 id="data-collected-heading">2. What Personal Data We Collect</h2>
    <p>
      The online enquiry form requires your name, email address, message and an
      acknowledgement that you have read this Privacy Policy. You may also
      provide a phone or WhatsApp number, requested service, vessel type, vessel
      length, vessel location, preferred date and uploaded files.
    </p>
    <p>
      We may also receive information you include voluntarily in messages,
      yacht-listing URLs, survey or yacht-delivery calculator summaries,
      estimate references, technical security information generated during
      submission, subsequent email correspondence, and business records created
      if you instruct a service.
    </p>
    <p class="policy-callout">
      Do not upload identification documents, financial information, medical
      information or other unnecessary sensitive personal data unless
      specifically requested through an agreed secure process.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="calculator-data" aria-labelledby="calculator-data-heading">
    <h2 id="calculator-data-heading">3. Calculator Data</h2>
    <p>
      Survey and delivery calculator results are initially saved in your
      browser’s <code>sessionStorage</code>. The website validates a stored
      result for up to 24 hours, while the storage itself is limited to the
      browser session. These records contain route, vessel, option and estimate
      information, but no Contact-form name, email, phone or message.
    </p>
    <p>
      Calculator data is brought into the Contact form only when you request a
      quotation. Refreshing a calculator or policy page does not submit an
      enquiry. <code>sessionStorage</code> is not a cookie, and you may remove a transferred
      summary before sending the form. Anyone with access to your browser session
      or device may be able to see locally stored information.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="uses" aria-labelledby="uses-heading">
    <h2 id="uses-heading">4. How We Use Personal Data</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Responding to enquiries and preparing quotations.</li>
      <li>Taking steps you request before a service agreement.</li>
      <li>Arranging surveys, inspections and yacht-delivery work.</li>
      <li>
        Communicating about and delivering an instructed service or report.
      </li>
      <li>Reviewing uploaded documents, yacht links and images.</li>
      <li>Maintaining relevant business and correspondence records.</li>
      <li>Preventing spam, abuse and security incidents.</li>
      <li>
        Establishing or defending legal claims and meeting legal obligations.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      All Yacht Service does not currently use Contact-form information for
      email marketing.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="legal-bases" aria-labelledby="legal-bases-heading">
    <h2 id="legal-bases-heading">5. Legal Bases</h2>
    <p>
      Depending on the circumstances, processing may be necessary to take steps
      you request before entering a contract, to perform an agreed contract, or
      to comply with a legal obligation. Processing may also rely on legitimate
      interests in answering business enquiries, operating and securing the
      website, maintaining proportionate records, preventing abuse and
      protecting legal rights, balanced against your interests and rights.
    </p>
    <p>
      Consent is used only where a genuinely optional activity requires it. The
      required acknowledgement beside the Contact form records that this notice
      was presented; it does not make consent the legal basis for every enquiry.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section
    id="required-information"
    aria-labelledby="required-information-heading"
  >
    <h2 id="required-information-heading">
      6. Required and Optional Information
    </h2>
    <p>
      Name, email, message and the privacy-notice acknowledgement are required
      for an online enquiry. Optional fields help prepare a more relevant
      response. You may instead contact us by phone, WhatsApp or email. Without
      essential information, we may be unable to assess a request or prepare a
      quotation.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="attachments" aria-labelledby="attachments-heading">
    <h2 id="attachments-heading">7. Attachments</h2>
    <p>
      The form accepts up to three PDF, JPEG, PNG or WebP files. Each file may
      be no larger than 2 MB, and all files together may be no larger than 3 MB.
      File type, extension, size and signature are checked by the server, and
      accepted files may be delivered with the enquiry email.
    </p>
    <p>
      You must have authority to share submitted material. Uploading does not
      transfer ownership. Remove unnecessary personal information before
      uploading and use an agreed secure process if sensitive material is
      specifically required.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="recipients" aria-labelledby="recipients-heading">
    <h2 id="recipients-heading">8. Service Providers and Recipients</h2>
    <p>Information may be handled by:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Cloudflare for website delivery, security and Turnstile.</li>
      <li>Google Workspace for email delivery and mailbox storage.</li>
      <li>Technical providers necessary to operate or secure the website.</li>
      <li>Professional advisers where necessary.</li>
      <li>
        Survey, repair or specialist professionals where you instruct or
        authorise this.
      </li>
      <li>Public authorities where disclosure is legally required.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Information is not shared with Premium Yachts Spain merely because
      Aleksandrs Tolkacovs has a commercial role there. Any relevant sharing or
      relationship must have an appropriate purpose and be disclosed where
      applicable.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="turnstile" aria-labelledby="turnstile-heading">
    <h2 id="turnstile-heading">9. Cloudflare Turnstile</h2>
    <p>
      Turnstile protects the Contact form from automated abuse. Browser-based
      checks produce a verification token which the server validates with
      Cloudflare before accepting the enquiry. Cloudflare may process technical
      browser, device, network and interaction signals for this purpose. All
      Yacht Service does not use Turnstile for advertising.
    </p>
    <p>
      The Contact page uses Cloudflare’s implicit widget rendering with the
      action <code>contact</code> and a light theme. The repository does not set an
      invisible or non-interactive mode and does not configure pre-clearance; the
      widget type and account-level pre-clearance setting must be confirmed in the
      Cloudflare dashboard before production. Storage behaviour can vary with that
      configuration, so this policy does not claim Turnstile is cookie-free in every
      possible setup.
    </p>
    <p>
      Read Cloudflare’s
      <a
        href="https://www.cloudflare.com/turnstile-privacy-policy/"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer">Turnstile Privacy Addendum (external link)</a
      >.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="google-workspace" aria-labelledby="google-workspace-heading">
    <h2 id="google-workspace-heading">10. Google Workspace</h2>
    <p>
      Form submissions are delivered to
      <a href={`mailto:${legalConfig.email}`}>{legalConfig.email}</a>. Email
      content and attachments may be stored in the Google Workspace mailbox and
      accessed by authorised mailbox users. Google processes this data under the
      applicable service and data-processing terms. No particular Google data
      region or transfer mechanism is asserted here because the account and
      contract settings require confirmation.
    </p>
    <p>
      See Google’s current
      <a
        href="https://cloud.google.com/terms/data-processing-addendum/"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
        >Cloud Data Processing Addendum (external link)</a
      >.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section
    id="international-transfers"
    aria-labelledby="international-transfers-heading"
  >
    <h2 id="international-transfers-heading">
      11. International Data Transfers
    </h2>
    <p>
      Some service providers may process or support personal data from locations
      outside the European Economic Area. Where required, transfers are handled
      using applicable contractual or legal safeguards made available by the
      relevant provider.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="retention" aria-labelledby="retention-heading">
    <h2 id="retention-heading">12. Data Retention</h2>
    {
      legalConfig.enquiryRetentionMonths !== null &&
      legalConfig.unsuccessfulQuoteRetentionMonths !== null &&
      legalConfig.clientRecordRetentionDescription &&
      legalConfig.securityRecordRetentionDescription ? (
        <ul>
          <li>
            General enquiries that do not become assignments are retained for up
            to {legalConfig.enquiryRetentionMonths} months after the last
            substantive contact.
          </li>
          <li>
            Unsuccessful quotations are retained for up to{' '}
            {legalConfig.unsuccessfulQuoteRetentionMonths} months after the
            quotation expires or the last substantive contact, whichever is
            later.
          </li>
          <li>
            Active client correspondence, reports and instructed-service
            records: {legalConfig.clientRecordRetentionDescription}
          </li>
          <li>
            Security and spam-prevention records:{' '}
            {legalConfig.securityRecordRetentionDescription}
          </li>
        </ul>
      ) : (
        <p>
          Final retention periods are awaiting approval and this draft cannot be
          published as an indexable policy until they are configured. The final
          schedule will distinguish general enquiries, unsuccessful quotations,
          active client correspondence, instructed-service records and reports,
          attachments, security records, and records required for legal, tax or
          accounting duties.
        </p>
      )
    }
    <p>
      Attachments follow the retention of the enquiry, mailbox correspondence or
      instructed-service record to which they relate. Records may be kept longer
      where a legal, tax, accounting, limitation-period or legal-claims duty
      requires it. Retention is based on whether an enquiry becomes an
      assignment, the record’s purpose, report-reliance considerations, security
      needs and mandatory record-keeping duties.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="security" aria-labelledby="security-heading">
    <h2 id="security-heading">13. Security</h2>
    <p>
      Appropriate technical and organisational measures are used to reduce
      unauthorised access, alteration, loss or disclosure. Verified controls
      include HTTPS, server-side input and file validation, Turnstile, file
      restrictions, restricted mailbox access and credentials stored in
      deployment environment settings. No method of transmission or storage can
      guarantee absolute security.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="rights" aria-labelledby="rights-heading">
    <h2 id="rights-heading">14. Your Rights</h2>
    <p>
      Depending on the circumstances, you may have rights of access,
      rectification, erasure, restriction, objection and data portability. You
      may withdraw consent where consent is the legal basis, without affecting
      earlier lawful processing. Contact
      <a href={`mailto:${legalConfig.privacyContactEmail}`}
        >{legalConfig.privacyContactEmail}</a
      >. Reasonable identity verification may be requested before acting on a
      request.
    </p>
    <p>
      You may also complain to the
      <a href="https://www.aepd.es/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
        >Spanish Data Protection Agency (AEPD) (external link)</a
      >.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section
    id="automated-decisions"
    aria-labelledby="automated-decisions-heading"
  >
    <h2 id="automated-decisions-heading">15. Automated Decision-Making</h2>
    <p>
      All Yacht Service does not use Contact-form information for automated
      decision-making or profiling that produces legal or similarly significant
      effects. Calculator outputs are automated estimates, but do not decide
      whether a service is accepted and do not constitute a quotation or
      contract.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="third-party-links" aria-labelledby="third-party-links-heading">
    <h2 id="third-party-links-heading">16. Third-Party Links</h2>
    <p>
      External websites, including Premium Yachts Spain and social networks,
      control their own content and privacy practices. Review their notices
      before submitting information to them.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="changes" aria-labelledby="changes-heading">
    <h2 id="changes-heading">17. Changes to This Policy</h2>
    <p>
      This notice may be updated when website functions, providers or legal
      requirements change. The review date at the top will be updated when a
      material revision is made.
    </p>
  </section>
</PolicyPageLayout>
